{
  "id": 472418165,
  "iid": 24289,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTITCP: Fix TCP reassembly of large RTPS data messages",
  "description": "get_rtitcp_pdu_len() read only a 16-bit length field, but RTPS data\nmessages encode their length in the 30 least-significant bits of the\nfirst four bytes. Messages larger than 65535 bytes (e.g. large data\nsamples over TCP) caused tcp_dissect_pdus() to desynchronize the\nstream, leaving all subsequent DATA submessages undecoded.\n\nAlso fix dissect_rtitcp_common() to use the 30-bit length for\ntvb_set_reported_length() and proto_item_set_len(), preventing the\nreassembled tvb from being truncated back to the wrong 16-bit size.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (GitHub Copilot)",
  "state": "merged",
